{
  "id": "multiagent-coder",
  "name": "Multi-agent coder — chat entry (runs pipeline)",
  "description": "Chat-agent entrypoint for the multi-agent coding pipeline (scouts -> plan -> gates -> build/verify loop -> docs -> PR -> merge). Defaults to gating_mode=wait: interactive clients answer TWO ask_user gates (plan approval, merge approval). Unattended clients must send gating_mode=auto and input_data._runtime.tool_policy = {\"auto_approve_max_risk_rank\": 2, \"auto_approve_tools\": [\"execute_command\", \"list_files\", \"read_file\", \"browser_probe\"]} (or drive approvals externally): the rank ceiling auto-approves the agents' read/skim tools, the names cover the pipeline's call_tool steps. workspace_root resolves from the session workspace var or input_data; an empty workspace is refused at preflight (this workflow writes files and runs git).",
  "interfaces": [
    "abstractcode.agent.v1"
  ],
